From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 17:06:35 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] tests: require finalized Dogecoin templates to retain
 dependency order

Optional preconsensus finalization does not enable CTOR consensus. Preserve exact selected transaction assertions while computing their deterministic dependency order from explicit fixture edges. Check parent-before-child order in the long capacity chain and both small selection fixtures, and verify repeated templates retain the same transaction order. These assertions exercise real sequential UTXO validation rather than enabling CTOR in the fixture.

